### 1. Get all tables
GET http://localhost:5000/api/tables

### 2. Create a valid table (Table 13)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/tables
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tableNumber": 13,
  "capacity": 4,
  "location": "Garden Area"
}

### 3. Create a duplicate table number (should fail: 409)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/tables
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tableNumber": 5,
  "capacity": 4,
  "location": "Main Hall"
}

### 4. Create with invalid data (should fail: 400)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/tables
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tableNumber": 0,
  "capacity": 50,
  "location": ""
}

### 5. Mark Table 11 as available again
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/tables/t11
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "available"
}

### 6. Update with an invalid status (should fail: 400)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/tables/t5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "broken"
}

### 7. Change Table 6's number to 5 (should fail: 409, number taken)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/tables/t6
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tableNumber": 5
}

### 8. Update a table that does not exist (should fail: 404)
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/tables/t99
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "capacity": 4
}

### 9. Send broken JSON (should fail: 400, handled by error middleware)
POST http://localhost:5000/api/tables
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tableNumber": 14, "capacity": }
